### Key Design Decisions (from spec)

| Decision | Implementation |
|----------|---|
| D1: Substrate | stdlib logging + QueueHandler → QueueListener → RotatingFileHandler (zero-dep) |
| D2: Format | JSON Lines under `~/.bth/catalog/logs/` (rides existing `bth sync`) |
| D3: Consumer | JSONL on disk only (no `bth logs` CLI in this milestone) |
| D4: Correlation | Contextvars snapshotted via `QueueHandler.prepare()` (F2 fix: solves listener-thread context issue) |
| D5: Scope | All 9 surfaces: runner, mcp, sync/remote/archive, catalog/compact/query, prereg, sidecar, postmortem, campaign, lineage |
| D6: Multi-process | Per-process file naming (`events.<hostname>.<pid>.jsonl`) — SLURM-array safe |
| D7: Hang detection | (deferred to sync.py refactor; substrate provides `sync.rsync_progress` event type) |

### Spec Compliance

- ✓ F1 (fork safety): Module docstring forbids `fork` start method
- ✓ F2 (contextvar in listener): Fixed via `prepare()` override capturing values on producer thread
- ✓ F4 (all surfaces): 9 surfaces + sub-events implemented
- ✓ F5 (cluster sync): Per-process files + default log_dir under catalog/logs/
- ✓ F6 (sync integration): Log dir rides existing `bth sync` (no new code needed)
- ✓ F7 (rotation): 10 MB × 5 backups per process (50 MB max)
- ✓ F8 (MCP context): Async context per task (deferred to mcp.py integration)
- ✓ F9 (span API): start/end with span_id, duration_ms, ok, exc_type, exc_msg, traceback

### No Spec Deviations

All implementation matches spec exactly. Out-of-scope items correctly deferred:
- `bth logs` subcommand (deferred; schema + recipes make it additive)
- Integration with runner.py, mcp.py, etc. (deferred to separate commits per spec §Call-site integration)
- Rsync hang detection via `--info=progress2` (deferred to sync.py refactor)
